// Statistics: transmissions and publication (D.262-95/96/97/98/100).
//
// DEONTIC MAP: duties with computed deadlines.
// - D.262-95: the president transmits annual data before the end of
//   the first quarter to TWO recipients ("au représentant de l'Etat
//   dans le département et aux services statistiques"): one duty per
//   recipient, each firing on its own premises; the 2025-01-01
//   wording extends the scope to spouses and partners (four rules:
//   two recipients times back-to-back windows);
// - D.262-96: CNAF and CCMSA transmit quarterly data; the current
//   wording (month-end headcounts before the end of the second month
//   of the quarter) differs from the predecessor (four items before
//   quarter end): two rules;
// - D.262-97: CNAF and CCMSA transmit annual data; current (31
//   December headcounts before the end of the third quarter) versus
//   predecessor (five items before the end of the first quarter):
//   two rules;
// - D.262-98: L.262-55 information to the statistical services, body
//   side and department side, for sample persons only
//   ("informations relatives aux personnes physiques destinées à la
//   constitution d'échantillons statistiquement représentatifs",
//   L.262-55; echantillon_l262_55): a filed claim alone does not
//   prove sample inclusion;
// - D.262-100: regular publication of the results, statistical
//   services and national funds ("assurent la publication régulière
//   des résultats de l'exploitation des données"); standing duties
//   of the statistical services and the national funds themselves,
//   with no beneficiary: the text states no claim trigger and no
//   individual beneficiary, and no computable period for "régulière",
//   so the window stays standing;
// - D.262-99 (ministerial orders fixing the lists): source boundary,
//   B-RSA-ARRETE-LISTES, no rule.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.casf.rsa version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:rsa";

// `use self` is hand-maintained in nochecks authoring (no `law fix
// imports` until the locks free). Fragment names join the block via the
// deferred `law fix imports fr.casf.rsa` run after regenerating sources.
